name: Link Analysis trade showcase
tagline: "A seeded trade-based money-laundering Link Analysis demo - over-invoicing between two companies that share a director, six containers shipped round a circle of three companies, letters of credit paid on bills of lading naming a vessel that was elsewhere, and six new importers at one formation-agent address paying one exporter, planted among 2 500 companies, 12 000 trades and 300 vessels with benign look-alikes"
description: "The trade-finance compliance Link Analysis demo as a Space Template, Basic tier. Seven synthetic feeds (trade_company, director, trade, bill_of_lading, vessel_position, price_reference, trade_payment; register snapshots and 12 months from 2025-10-01 in data/inbox, October 2026 in data/staged; 2 500 companies, about 12 000 letters of credit and collections, 12 000 bills of lading, 300 invented vessels with a position every day, 62 real HS codes with invented reference prices and about 29 000 payments) are landed by seven Collectors and Pipelines. The trade_links Job folds them into ONE link Dataset (src, dst, kind, ts, amount, event_date, via, flag) of six link kinds: traded_with, on_vessel, shipped_in, directed_by, registered_at and paid; flag marks the red flags, among them vessel_elsewhere, a bill of lading whose vessel was not in its port of loading on the B/L date (vessel_position joined on vessel and date). Four Jobs derive one Dataset per saved view. Planted stories (ground truth: tools/gen-la-trade-data.ground-truth.json; pinned by TradeLinksJobGoldenTest and tools/gen-la-trade-data.test.mjs): 14 shipments of integrated circuits at 3 to 8 times the reference price between a Hong Kong exporter and a UK importer that share a director; the same 6 containers shipped twice round three companies in the UAE, India and Malaysia in 4 months, the value rising each leg; 5 letters of credit paid on bills of lading naming a vessel that was elsewhere; 6 importers incorporated within 2 months at one London formation-agent address, paying one Chinese exporter about 36 times what it shipped them. Benign look-alikes that must not join a story: a specialty supplier priced steadily over 3 times the reference, a leasing pool's boxes carried for many shippers, transhipments whose trade names the second vessel, and long-standing companies at a large business centre. Four saved views, one per story. Runs on every edition, Basic included: no sign-in personas, Alert Rules or Investigations. Synthetic data only; every company, person, vessel, port and container is invented."
minEdition: basic
icon: heroicons_outline:globe-alt
contents[5]: "7 Collectors + Pipelines + Datasets (register snapshots, 12 months landed, 1 month staged)", "trade_links Job + Dataset (6 link kinds, red-flag column)", "Bill of lading checked against the vessel's position on the B/L date", "4 saved views, each on its own derived Dataset (over-invoicing, phantom shipment, circular trade, shell importers)", "4 planted stories with benign look-alikes"
